The built plugin (dist/plugin.js) bundles buzz-app modules unchanged at the
revision in scripts/build-plugin.mjs (BUZZ_APP_REV): among them
src/bundled/goose/runtime.ts, src/bundled/goose/run.ts,
src/bundled/goose/sessions.ts,
src/features/agent-harness/acp/, src/features/agents/ActivityTranscript.tsx and
src/buzz-mcp/, and the design system with its DeepSeek mark. The DeepSeek mark
is DeepSeek's, MIT-licensed, as buzz-app's NOTICE.md says.

Through them the build holds the noble-curves, noble-hashes, noble-ciphers and
scure-base libraries by Paul Miller, and parts of React and React DOM, Base UI,
Floating UI, Motion, Tabler Icons, react-markdown and remark-gfm (with the
unified, micromark and mdast libraries they use), each licensed under the MIT
License (@ungap/structured-clone: ISC). Their license notices stay in the build. The build replaces three modules with
this repository's own (see the SWAPS list there).

These files repeat or adapt buzz-app code; each marks it in a comment:

- src/dsh.ts: the process adapter shape of src/bundled/goose/goose.ts, its
  steering hook included.
- src/sessions.ts: wraps src/bundled/goose/sessions.ts, and adapts its
  SharedProcess.
- src/index.ts: the agent type and sessions list of
  src/bundled/goose/index.ts.
- src/views.tsx: the New agent and Settings views of
  src/bundled/goose/tabs.tsx, built from the same buzz-app components.
- src/provider.tsx: the provider row and dialog of
  src/bundled/goose/tabs.tsx.
- src/activity.tsx: the Activity tab of src/bundled/goose/tabs.tsx.
- src/session-files.ts: the reading of a harness's sessions of
  src/bundled/goose/transcript.ts.
- tsconfig.json: the compiler options of buzz-app's tsconfig.json.

The build also bundles @hpcc-js/wasm-zstd by HPCC Systems, licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0, for the transcripts. It holds a WebAssembly build
of Zstandard by Meta Platforms, Inc., licensed under the BSD License:
https://github.com/facebook/zstd

DeepSeek Harness (dsh) is a separate program. This plugin does not include
it; it starts the copy that the user installed. This plugin is not
affiliated with or endorsed by DeepSeek or Block, Inc.
